      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_ae42677c97bf2de78a4eccab60516c5928b96bae59db89f93f92d2e75b78dc5c",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The implementation changes its retained object from a high-precision zero database to the minimum local information needed for counting: after detecting a sign change, it does not zoom in with Shannon–Whittaker–Nyquist machinery or store a refined zero. Arb also reduces memory relative to MPFI, and the default lattice empirically isolates nearly all zeros directly. This span supports the efficiency tradeoff only; it does not contain the surrounding global completeness argument, so sign changes alone must not be described here as a complete certificate.",
